A||||8||Adrift||Video Gurus: How to hook up SVHS to a regular tV? ||||5||
Z||000000||Adrift||11-08-2001||11:41 PM||||My TV doesn't have SVHS in but my laptop only has SVHS out - is there any way to convert SVHS to RCA cables or something so I can use my laptop with a non SVHS tv?||||reg||5
Z||000001||fierospeeder||11-08-2001||11:57 PM||||are you talking about S-video or SVHS.<P>SVHS is a video format.  Regular vhs tapes at ?? 300 resolution and SVHS tapes at 400-500 resolution.   this is out of memory so resolutions might not be correct.<BR>JVC sells videorecorders that tape in SVHS.<P>S-video is a video connection that is round and has 5-7? pins that hooks directly to the tv.  It has no sound, just video.  I believe theres a cable where you can make svideo turn into a normal rca video cable.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Adrift||11-09-2001||12:14 AM||||Sorry SVIDEO cable - can I splice one to turn it into a RCA cable?||||reg||1
Z||000003||fierospeeder||11-09-2001||12:31 AM||||i guess you can try it.<P>Ive seen the converter.  Its just a S video on one end and a single rca plug on the other.  <P>It might/might not work, because theres more wires on the svideo then rca, if your going to splice it.  Unless you want to stop at radioshack||||reg||1
